cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Intraday Volume Anomaly: the 10:15-10:30 ET Window in CME Futures
  - a preregistered study
message: >-
  If you use, quote, or build on this work, please cite it as below.
  Attribution is the sole condition of the license.
type: dataset
authors:
  - alias: nattobbm
    website: https://github.com/nattobbm
repository-code: https://github.com/nattobbm/gold-es
url: https://github.com/nattobbm/gold-es/blob/main/results.md
abstract: >-
  A preregistered, fully reproducible study of a recurring intraday volume
  surge in the 10:15-10:30 ET window across four CME futures contracts
  (ES, MES, GC, MGC). The specification and analysis script were publicly
  frozen on 2026-07-23, before the confirmatory sample existed, and their
  SHA256 hashes were committed to the Bitcoin blockchain on 2026-08-03
  (block 960824). The confirmatory sample of 30 qualifying trading days
  closed 2026-08-25; the frozen test was run once on 2026-08-31. Both
  preregistered hypotheses were confirmed out of sample: the 10:15-10:30
  bucket volume z-score exceeds zero in all four contracts, and micro
  contracts show a higher z-score than their full-size counterparts.
  Effect sizes attenuated relative to the exploratory sample, as expected
  given the declared post-hoc bucket selection. The mechanism is unresolved.
keywords:
  - preregistration
  - reproducible research
  - market microstructure
  - intraday volume seasonality
  - futures
  - CME
  - open science
license-url: https://github.com/nattobbm/gold-es/blob/main/LICENSE
date-released: '2026-08-31'
version: '1.0'
identifiers:
  - type: other
    value: 'git commit 9a59771'
    description: >-
      Preregistration commit, 2026-07-23, predating the confirmatory sample.
  - type: other
    value: 'Bitcoin block 960824'
    description: >-
      Block mined 2026-08-03 05:05:26 UTC containing the OpenTimestamps
      attestation of the frozen files' SHA256 hashes.
